##   SIMPLE:   se = sqrt(SSR / (n - 2)) / sqrt(SST_X)
##   MULTIPLE: se = sigma-hat / sqrt( SST_j * (1 - R_j^2) )
##     j    = the x whose coefficient you want the se of
##     SST_j = total variation of THAT x:  sum((xj - mean(xj))^2)
##     R_j^2 = R^2 from regressing xj on the OTHER x's.  y is NEVER in it.
