## [B6] WHAT MAKES Var(bj-hat) = sigma^2 / [SST_j (1 - R_j^2)] BIGGER?  (no computing)
##   bigger sigma^2 (noisier errors)                              -> BIGGER
##   smaller SST_j (x bunched together, or fewer observations)    -> BIGGER
##   bigger R_j^2 (xj more correlated with other x's)             -> BIGGER; R_j^2 -> 1: grows without bound
##   more observations / more spread-out x                        -> SMALLER
##   the size of the true beta, the intercept                     -> NO effect
##   Why prefer smaller variance: estimates land closer to beta from sample to sample (PS10 #5)


